  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Advancing Girls&apos; Education</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">USAID Promovendo a Educa&#xe7;&#xe3;o de Meninas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mozambique):  .The Education Ministry&apos;s ten-year strategic plan (2020-2029).recognizes that Mozambican schools generally fail to provide a safe and.supportive learning environment for children, especially for girls..Furthermore, poor learning facilities, unsafe learning environments, and sexual.related gender-based violence (GBV) add to school insecurity for female.students. Child marriage also contributes to school dropout and poor learning.outcomes.With FY 2022 funds, the Advancing Girls&apos; Education (AGE).activity will increase access to school for girls between the ages 10-19 and.increase community support for girls&apos; education. Using radio, cultural events,.and social media, AGE will raise awareness of parents, guardians, and community.leaders about the importance of girls&apos; education for their livelihoods, families,.and communities. Activities will also train teachers in inclusive teaching.methods to improve girls&apos; performance in upper primary and secondary schools..AGE will work with USAID&apos;s Determined, Resilient, Empowered, AIDS-free,.Mentored, and Safe (DREAMS) activity, Integrated Family Planning Project.(IFPP), Social and Behavior Change Communication (SBCC) activity, and other.supply chain programs delivering messages aiming to increase girls&apos; access to.key social services such as health and WASH, and reduce violence and gender.inequality. AGE will promote safe school and household environments to reduce.girls&apos; vulnerability to early marriage and pregnancy, sexually transmitted.diseases, and school related GBV. AGE will support the use of school-based.health committee and community health worker platforms to prevent early child.marriage, promote the adoption of key healthy behaviors, including counselling.and referrals for family planning and GBV response in school and in the.household..</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">(Mo&#xe7;ambique): O plano estrat&#xe9;gico decenal do Minist&#xe9;rio da Educa&#xe7;&#xe3;o (2020-2029). reconhece que as escolas mo&#xe7;ambicanas geralmente n&#xe3;o conseguem proporcionar um ambiente de aprendizagem seguro e favor&#xe1;vel &#xe0;s crian&#xe7;as, especialmente &#xe0;s raparigas. O casamento infantil tamb&#xe9;m contribui para o abandono escolar e para os maus resultados de aprendizagem. Com os fundos do exerc&#xed;cio financeiro de 2022, a actividade Avan&#xe7;ar a Educa&#xe7;&#xe3;o das Raparigas (AGE) aumentar&#xe1; o acesso &#xe0; escola para as raparigas entre os 10 e os 19 anos de idade e aumentar&#xe1; o apoio comunit&#xe1;rio &#xe0; educa&#xe7;&#xe3;o das raparigas. Utilizando r&#xe1;dio, eventos culturais e meios de comunica&#xe7;&#xe3;o social, a AGE ir&#xe1; sensibilizar os pais, tutores e l&#xed;deres comunit&#xe1;rios sobre a import&#xe2;ncia da educa&#xe7;&#xe3;o das raparigas para a sua subsist&#xea;ncia, fam&#xed;lias e comunidades. As actividades tamb&#xe9;m ir&#xe3;o formar professores em m&#xe9;todos de ensino inclusivos para melhorar o desempenho das raparigas nas escolas prim&#xe1;rias e secund&#xe1;rias. desigualdade.de g&#xea;nero. A AGE promover&#xe1; ambientes escolares e dom&#xe9;sticos seguros para reduzir a vulnerabilidade das raparigas ao casamento e &#xe0; gravidez precoces, &#xe0;s doen&#xe7;as sexualmente transmiss&#xed;veis e &#xe0; viol&#xea;ncia baseada no g&#xe9;nero relacionada com a escola. A AGE apoiar&#xe1; a utiliza&#xe7;&#xe3;o de plataformas de comit&#xe9;s de sa&#xfa;de escolares e de profissionais de sa&#xfa;de comunit&#xe1;rios para prevenir o casamento infantil precoce, promover a adop&#xe7;&#xe3;o de comportamentos saud&#xe1;veis &#x200b;&#x200b;essenciais, incluindo aconselhamento.e encaminhamentos para planeamento familiar e resposta &#xe0; VBG na escola e no agregado familiar..</narrative>
  </description>
